WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.908
Sequence analysis depends on order A timestamp
usually defines

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:11.613
the main sequence If two events share the same
timestamp a stable event

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:17.336
ID can break the tie Without a meaningful order
previous and next

00:00:17.362 --> 00:00:22.921
are undefined from an analytical perspective Always
treat the ordering

00:00:22.947 --> 00:00:25.039
clause as part of the business logic
